  "notes": "priority 3 (dictionary_word_list.word + enemy_name_template + minigame_shogi + word_list). 250 keys, ~230 are plain Japanese-surname transliterations (ambient NPC/shogi-opponent name pool). ~20 are enemy nicknames/boss labels: elemental Generals (Water/Fire/Sky/Wind -> แม่ทัพธาตุน้ำ/ไฟ/ฟ้า/ลม), Four Guardian Beasts Genbu/Byakko/Seiryu (transliterated, EN was romaji not English gloss), Tengu nicknames (Sagami Tengu/Karasu Tengu -> [place/epithet]+เท็งงุ, matching existing lock 'Mito Tengu style'=สำนักมิโตะเท็งงุ), real Bakumatsu-era assassins Kawakami Gensai / Tanaka Shinbei (surname transliterated per existing surname convention in this same list), and English-phrase mob labels (Bear, Quick Man, Man with Gun, Broke-Looking Ronin, Urayama Henchman) translated by meaning. Dark Ebisu and Komuso used exact existing glossary locks (เอบิสึมืด / โคมุโซ). NOTE for lead: despite source list including 'locres:minigame_shogi', none of these 250 strings are actual shogi piece/move/state terminology (no 歩/金/銀/王手/詰み/成る/持ち駒 found in ref_ja) -- they are the pool of shogi-opponent portrait names + a general surname word-list. The real shogi vocabulary set (piece names, promote/check/checkmate/captured-pieces-in-hand) has not yet appeared in any batch seen so far; flagging so it isn't assumed already covered.\n[lead 2 ก.ย. 2026] Suzui (す-ず-い) = สุซึอิ — เดิมเขียน 'ซึซุอิ' สลับ す กับ ず · ยึดผลของ scripts/romaji_to_thai.py\n[lead 2 ก.ย. 2026] check_cross_batch รอบปิดคลื่น: Makino = มากิโนะ (ka กลางคำใช้ ก) · Goro (五郎) = โกโร (สระยาวไม่เติม ะ) · Satcho (薩長) = ซัตโช (ちょ = โช)"
